     :measured "2026-09-02: upper-case-root agrees with String.toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT) over the sweep AND over 244 multi-code-point strings (44 hand-picked, 200 from seed 20260902), except where the host JDK's simple mapping is behind Unicode 16.0 -- then the published simple uppercase, asserted. The string sweep is separate because a claim about a string is not a claim about a character. The 102 SpecialCasing expansions (\u00df -> SS, \u0149 -> \u02bcN, \ufb01 -> FI) are in the table; simple-upper-case is the one-code-point mapping and leaves \u00df alone, which the oracle asserts."}
