     :measured-oracle "clojure.string/split's own behaviour, recorded so the eventual implementation has a target rather than a belief: (split \"a,b,,c,\" #\",\") is [\"a\" \"b\" \"\" \"c\"] -- trailing empties dropped; (split \"\" #\",\") is [\"\"]; (split \",a\" #\",\") is [\"\" \"a\"]; (split \",,,\" #\",\") is []; (split \"abc\" #\",\") is [\"abc\"]. Measured 2026-09-08, Clojure 1.12.4."}
    split-lines {:reason "same return as split: as many segments as the input has, and no way to build a list of unknown length (:measured :list-construction). Its separator question is smaller than split's -- it splits on a newline, optionally preceded by a carriage return, rather than on an arbitrary pattern -- so construction is the whole of what is left."}
